<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see rain only in northwest.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see rain only in northwest.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies to see rain in the northwest but sunny and warm weather everywhere else, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see rain in the Peace River Valley and highs of 18 to 22 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see rain in the central region, sun elsewhere, with highs of 18 to 26 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see a mix of sun and cloud with highs of 18 to 26 Celsius.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
